    rdfs:label "Evidence for Cardamom used in Pharmaceuticals & Druggists' Preparations: P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Products of the Vegetable Kingdom (1854; Project Gutenberg #15191), section CARDAMOMS"@en ;
    <ontology/quoteText/#resource> "CARDAMOMS: Cardamoms are the production of various species of plants of the same tribe as the ginger, and might be profitably cultivated with that aromatic root, as well as the Turmeric (Curcuma longa), which see. Various species of Alpiniae, Amomum, Elettaria, and Renealmia, appear to furnish the cardamoms of the shops, which consist of the oval, trivalvula..."@en ;
